```

So, translated:

- no previous `BR_SPAWN_LOOPER` request is still outstanding/unclaimed (`requested_thread_count == 0`) — and the increment ensures at most one outstanding request;
- no already-registered looper is idle and waiting for work (`ready_threads` is empty, i.e. no thread is available to take the process work queue);
- the number of started/registered pool threads is still below the process maximum (`started_thread_count < max_threads`), where `max_threads` is set by userspace via `BINDER_SET_MAX_THREADS` (default 0, so no request is made until userspace raises it).

The counter is decremented when a new thread performs `BC_REGISTER_LOOPER` (`ProcessInner::register_thread`), which also increments `started_thread_count`.

**Directory:** `drivers/android/binder/` — the Rust Binder driver is the `drivers/android/binder/*.rs` tree (e.g. `thread.rs`, `process.rs`, `node.rs`, `transaction.rs`, `allocation.rs`, …).

**Where it asks for a new looper:** the `read()` method of `Thread` (i.e. `Thread::read`) in **`drivers/android/binder/thread.rs`**. At the end of the read it emits `BR_SPAWN_LOOPER`.

```rust
